The source supports a larger gap than bridge wiring: the interrupt flag has two writes and no reads, the kernel-entry array has no dispatching reads, and PAL interrupt return is unimplemented. I also found two routes into the LCA endpoint: ISA aggregation and direct PIC output changes, including masking and end-of-interrupt handling.
